Analyzing Performance Metrics
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Install and configure Prometheus for system monitoring
Install and configure Grafana for data visualization
Write complex PromQL queries to analyze CPU, memory, and network usage
Create comprehensive Grafana dashboards to visualize performance metrics
Interpret performance data to identify system bottlenecks and trends
Understand the relationship between different system metrics
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with system monitoring concepts (CPU, memory, network)
Basic knowledge of web browsers and HTTP protocols
Understanding of YAML configuration files
Basic networking concepts (ports, localhost, IP addresses)
