Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Prometheus Not Starting
Symptoms: Service fails to start or immediately stops

Solutions:

Check configuration syntax:
sudo /usr/local/bin/promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Check service logs:
sudo journalctl -u prometheus -f
Verify file permissions:
sudo chown -R prometheus:prometheus /etc/prometheus
sudo chown -R prometheus:prometheus /var/lib/prometheus
Issue 2: No Data in Grafana
Symptoms: Dashboards show "No data" or empty graphs

Solutions:

Verify Prometheus is collecting data:
curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=up
Check Node Exporter is running:
curl http://localhost:9100/metrics
Verify data source configuration in Grafana
Issue 3: High Resource Usage
Symptoms: System becomes slow or unresponsive

Solutions:

Adjust scrape intervals in prometheus.yml
Reduce retention time:
--storage.tsdb.retention.time=7d
Limit memory usage:
--storage.tsdb.retention.size=1GB
Performance Analysis Interpretation
CPU Metrics Analysis
Normal Range: 0-70% for general workloads
Warning Range: 70-85% sustained usage
Critical Range: Above 85% for extended periods
Key Indicators:

High iowait suggests disk bottlenecks
High system time indicates kernel overhead
High user time shows application load
Memory Metrics Analysis
Available Memory: Should be above 15% of total
Buffer/Cache: Normal to see high usage
Swap Usage: Should remain minimal (< 10%)
Key Indicators:

Consistent swap usage indicates memory pressure
Rapid memory growth suggests memory leaks
Low available memory affects system performance
Network Metrics Analysis
Baseline Traffic: Establish normal patterns
Error Rates: Should be near zero
Dropped Packets: Indicates network congestion
Key Indicators:

Sudden traffic spikes may indicate issues
High error rates suggest hardware problems
Asymmetric traffic patterns need investigation
